  "interpretation_guardrails": [
    "Report proper scores and coverage together; a system cannot appear safe by abstaining on every case.",
    "Report mandatory-abstention compliance separately from optional abstentions.",
    "Brier score and log loss are primary proper scores; ECE is a bin-dependent diagnostic, not a standalone ranking metric.",
    "Do not compare models unless they use identical case IDs, outcome definitions, horizons, qualification states and evaluation splits.",
    "No calibration guarantee is inferred under distribution shift or non-exchangeable time-series data.",
    "Abstained cases do not receive invented probabilities and do not enter selective proper-score denominators.",
    "Never convert missing/conflicting/unsupported evidence into a zero breach probability."
  ]
}
